<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-6smd9voUY0VkyA6NT2acrI+jbKMEnJea/u0SMBWEj40='; style-src 'self' 'sha256-+TtOn0WMqNxdTCW3+OXOsV4XUmPzjroFqKEe8Zdoj0c='; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; media-src 'none'">
  <title>S143 — One original journey budget</title>
  <script>
  (() => {
    const param = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("clawpilotTheme");
    const theme =
      param || (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches ? "dark" : "light");
    document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-theme", theme);
  })();
  </script>
  <style>
:root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --cp-bg: #f7f4ef;
  --cp-bg-elevated: #fcfbf8;
  --cp-surface: #ffffff;
  --cp-surface-soft: #f5f5f5;
  --cp-border: #dedede;
  --cp-border-strong: #919191;
  --cp-text: #242424;
  --cp-text-muted: #5c5c5c;
  --cp-text-soft: #6f6f6f;
  --cp-accent: #b11f4b;
  --cp-accent-hover: #9a1a41;
  --cp-accent-soft: rgba(177, 31, 75, 0.08);
  --cp-accent-fg: #ffffff;
  --cp-success: #16a34a;
  --cp-danger: #dc2626;
  --cp-warning: #f59e0b;
  --cp-link: #0078d4;
  --cp-shadow: 0 18px 48px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  --cp-overlay: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
  --cp-panel: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.86);
  --cp-panel-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
  --cp-sheen: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
  --cp-highlight: rgba(177, 31, 75, 0.12);
}
html[data-theme="dark"] {
  color-scheme: dark;
  --cp-bg: #3d3b3a;
  --cp-bg-elevated: #343231;
  --cp-surface: #292929;
  --cp-surface-soft: #2e2e2e;
  --cp-border: #474747;
  --cp-border-strong: #5f5f5f;
  --cp-text: #dedede;
  --cp-text-muted: #919191;
  --cp-text-soft: #b0b0b0;
  --cp-accent: #fd8ea1;
  --cp-accent-hover: #fb7b91;
  --cp-accent-soft: rgba(253, 142, 161, 0.14);
  --cp-accent-fg: #1a1a1a;
  --cp-success: #4ade80;
  --cp-danger: #f87171;
  --cp-warning: #fbbf24;
  --cp-link: #4da6ff;
  --cp-shadow: 0 18px 48px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.32);
  --cp-overlay: rgba(41, 41, 41, 0.88);
  --cp-panel: rgba(41, 41, 41, 0.72);
  --cp-panel-strong: rgba(41, 41, 41, 0.96);
  --cp-sheen: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
  --cp-highlight: rgba(253, 142, 161, 0.12);
}
  </style>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="lesson.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <p class="banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
  <h1>S143: One original journey budget</h1>
  <p>Slow a client/reconnect; retries must remain inside the original journey budget.</p>
  <p class="notice"><strong>Fixed fictional teaching DATA ONLY.</strong> No live client, network, clock, traffic, load generator or user data. Buttons reveal supplied records immediately; they do not wait, reconnect or send anything.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="conduct-heading">
    <h2 id="conduct-heading">1. Conduct a fixed trace</h2>
    <p>Start → record slow-client interruption → record backoff/reconnect → inspect final attempt → measure the original journey. A short new attempt or HTTP 200 is not a fresh budget.</p>
    <p>Declared <em>teaching</em> support: one fictional client, at most two supplied attempts; first wait 800 ms, known final wait 200 ms, backoff 400 or 1101 ms, reconnect 300 or 600 ms, known final service 500 / 600 / 601 / 1300 ms. Null final timing stays unobserved. The outside-support preset is explicitly unsupported. These are closed DATA labels, not measured network capabilities.</p>
    <form id="controls">
      <label for="preset">Fixed slow-client condition</label>
      <select id="preset" name="preset">
        <option value="within-budget">Within budget — 2900 ms</option>
        <option value="exact-deadline">Exact deadline — 3000 ms</option>
        <option value="one-ms-over">One ms over — 3001 ms, short HTTP 200 attempt</option>
        <option value="per-attempt-reset">False per-attempt reset — 3700 ms</option>
        <option value="missing-final-time">Missing final time — UNKNOWN</option>
        <option value="missing-completion">Missing completion — UNKNOWN despite HTTP 200</option>
        <option value="late-unknown">Known late, unknown final — FAIL</option>
        <option value="reconnect-failed">Reconnect failed — FAIL</option>
        <option value="incorrect-200">Incorrect result despite HTTP 200 — FAIL</option>
        <option value="unsupported-condition">Outside supported condition — FAIL</option>
      </select>
      <div class="buttons">
        <button id="start" type="button" data-action="start">Start original journey</button>
        <button id="slow" type="button" data-action="slow" disabled>Record slow interruption</button>
        <button id="reconnect" type="button" data-action="reconnect" disabled>Record backoff / reconnect</button>
        <button id="observe" type="button" data-action="observe" disabled>Inspect final attempt</button>
        <button id="measure" type="button" data-action="measure" disabled>Measure original budget</button>
        <button id="reset-button" type="button" data-action="reset">Reset controls / retain history</button>
      </div>
    </form>
    <p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite" tabindex="-1">Loadable teaching stub; no result certified.</p>
    <p id="error" role="alert" aria-live="assertive" tabindex="-1"></p>
    <noscript>This lesson needs JavaScript. No result is certified while scripting is disabled.</noscript>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="inspect-heading">
    <h2 id="inspect-heading">2. Inspect immutable origin and cumulative DATA</h2>
    <dl class="metrics">
      <div><dt>Phase</dt><dd id="phase">idle</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Original start / deadline (fictional ms)</dt><dd><span id="start-ms">unobserved</span> / <span id="deadline-ms">unobserved</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Original budget (ms)</dt><dd id="budget-ms">unobserved</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Original completion time / elapsed (ms)</dt><dd><span id="completion-ms">unobserved</span> / <span id="elapsed-ms">unobserved</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Known cumulative elapsed lower bound (ms)</dt><dd id="known-ms">0</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Remaining at known observation (upper bound when unknown, ms)</dt><dd id="remaining-ms">unobserved</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Final attempt duration (diagnostic only, ms)</dt><dd id="attempt-ms">unobserved</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Short final attempt within 3000 ms? (not the verdict)</dt><dd id="per-attempt">unobserved</dd></div>
      <div><dt>HTTP result DATA / version DATA</dt><dd><span id="http-result">unobserved</span> / <span id="version">unobserved</span></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Retained original interruption count</dt><dd id="interruptions">0</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p><strong>Labeled condition:</strong> <span id="condition">unobserved</span></p>
    <p><strong>Observed native effect:</strong> <span id="native-result">unverified — not observed</span>. Fictional emulation DATA does not establish actual network behavior.</p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table><caption>Every supplied wait, attempt and reconnect stays in the original timeline</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Record</th><th scope="col">Version DATA</th><th scope="col">Wait / service / backoff / reconnect (ms)</th><th scope="col">Fictional observation time (ms)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="timeline"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <details><summary>Exact current trace / output shape (null is unknown)</summary><pre id="trace">null</pre></details>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="measure-heading">
    <h2 id="measure-heading">3. Measure the original journey</h2>
    <p>PASS requires supported conditions, recovered connection, known original completion at or before 4000 ms, HTTP result and correct completed state. Equality passes; 4001 ms fails. Unknown final completion/time is never filled in. A known cumulative overrun fails even if the final result is unknown.</p>
    <p class="result" id="verdict">UNKNOWN — not measured</p>
    <p><strong>User-impact DATA:</strong> <span id="impact">unknown</span></p>
    <p><strong>Preset verifier (separate from impact):</strong> <span id="verifier">not measured</span></p>
    <table><caption>Independent acceptance checks</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">Result</th><th scope="col">Evidence / rule</th></tr></thead><tbody id="assertions"></tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="history-heading">
    <h2 id="history-heading">Retained, bounded in-memory history</h2>
    <p><span id="run-count">0</span> / 12 runs; <span id="history-count">0</span> / 72 accepted actions; <span id="rejection-count">0</span> / 12 retained rejected actions; <span id="outcome-count">0</span> archived outcomes. Reset never erases these records. Reload intentionally starts a new nonpersistent teaching exercise.</p>
    <h3>Original journey outcomes</h3><ol id="outcomes"></ol>
    <details><summary>Accepted actions / original deadlines</summary><ol id="history"></ol></details>
    <details><summary>Sanitized rejected actions (first 12 only)</summary><ol id="rejections"></ol></details>
  </section>
  <footer>A-S143 · D-S143 · frozen Kano S · P1 · SC-S143 · SOURCE. Native B-S143 and source-parent acceptance remain blocked/unverified. No cloud, IaC, deployment, production Node 24 validation, five-nines or extra-credit claim. Educational AS-IS; see the repository's Microsoft Open Source Disclaimer.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
